.TH std::vector::~vector 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::vector::~vector \- std::vector::~vector

.SH Synopsis
~vector();  (constexpr since C++20)

A destructor. Destructs the vector. The destructors of the elements are called and the
used storage is deallocated. Note, that if the elements are pointers, the pointed-to
objects are not destroyed.

.SH Complexity

Linear in the size of the vector.
